{"name":"Golden Rule","hex":"#daae49","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden rule","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fundamental rule or principle.","The principle that one should treat other people in the manner in which one would want to be treated by them."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden_rule"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Rule","blocks":[{"text":"The Golden Rule is the principle of treating others as one would want to be treated by them. It is sometimes called an ethics of reciprocity, meaning that one should reciprocate to others how one would like them to treat the person. Various expressions of this rule can be found in the tenets of most religions and creeds through the ages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Golden_rule_sign_-_DPLA_-_49f451158847e00398bdb30ef4bf667f.jpg/330px-Golden_rule_sign_-_DPLA_-_49f451158847e00398bdb30ef4bf667f.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Rule","wikidata":"Q189573"},{"title":"Golden Rule (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Rule is the seventh and final studio album by Australian rock band Powderfinger, released on 13 November 2009. The album reunites the band with producer Nick DiDia, who produced several of the group's previous albums including, Internationalist, Odyssey Number Five and Vulture Street."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/Goldenrule01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Rule_(album)","wikidata":"Q5579764"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://e